# CLIB ROM jump-table definition (vectoring layer).
#
# Each non-comment, non-blank line names a ROM-resident public FUNCTION symbol
# that is exposed to applications through a fixed-address JMP slot in the ROM
# (segment JUMPTABLE, base $8100, 3 bytes per slot). Applications call the slot,
# which JMPs to the real (relocatable) function body, so the ROM code can move
# between builds without breaking already-linked application binaries.
#
# RULES (critical for binary compatibility):
#   * Order = slot index and is PERMANENT. Append new functions at the END only.
#   * NEVER reorder or delete a line. To retire a slot, replace the symbol with
#     the keyword RESERVED (keeps every later slot at its fixed address).
#   * Only list real functions (JMP targets), never data symbols.
#   * Every listed symbol must be ROM-resident (the generator errors otherwise).
#
# Slot 0 is the first line below.

_abs
_labs
_atoi
_atol
_itoa
_ltoa
_memcmp
_memcpy
_memmove
_memset
_strcat
_strchr
_strcmp
_strcpy
_strcspn
_strlen
_strncat
_strncmp
_strncpy
_strpbrk
_strrchr
_strspn
_strstr
_tolower
_toupper
